MATING MATERIAL IV RESUME 1.0.1
Prepared 30 October 2026, Toronto

SAVE AND RUN
Extract this folder in ~/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop, then run:
  bash "$HOME/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop/Mating_Material_IV_Resume_v1_0_1/RUN_IV_RESUME.command"

EXPECTED RUNTIME
Allow 2–5 hours provisionally, including verification, the unfinished score
sensitivities, and the entry/ordinary-ending comparisons. The previous partial
run took 5 hours 9 minutes; this launcher preserves its completed stages.
A fresh chronology scan or an unusually slow external drive can extend this.
Tests take approximately one minute. XT_Pro must be mounted. The existing
MatingMaterial_IV_Env_v100 environment is reused. Defaults: 10 workers maximum,
11 GiB memory, one BLAS thread, two heavy data jobs and sequential model fits.
The conservative startup free-space check remains 160 GiB. Caffeinate prevents
idle sleep on macOS. Keep the Mac plugged in.

WHAT WAS FIXED
1. The last-move-hour fixed effects exceeded 1,000 demeaning sweeps. Two-factor
   models now use a sparse normalized Schur solve with one gauge per connected
   component. The fixed-effect span, rows, controls and original group-mean
   tolerance are unchanged. Failed numerical certificates still stop the fit.
   Other models retain the original projection routine.
2. The completed chronology remainder is stored at
   PRIVATE/chronology_merge90/complete/features.parquet. The previous launcher
   looked one directory higher and combined only the cache hits. Both cache
   parts are now authenticated and their counts, uniqueness and exact row
   coverage are checked. Missing rows are not discarded or filled.

PRESERVING COMPLETED WORK
This repair targets only the reviewed partial run 12093d55b7ee9f73 at:
  __PRIVATE_VALUE_1__/derived/replication/
  mating_material_iv_batch_v100_PRIVATE/12093d55b7ee9f73
It will not create a new full rerun if that run is absent. The original package
and input data stay untouched. Its baseline configuration remains the cache
identity; REPAIR_V101.json separately records this execution repair and its
package hash. Completed public results, material inputs, saved frames and the
primary estimate are verified. The eleven completed stages are skipped.
Already completed sensitivity fits are checked and reused individually.
Run the same resume command after interruption; completed repair stages are
then skipped too. Checksums and dependency checks are not disabled.

The original all-time-five, both-role author exclusions, 90-day windows,
first-pair rules, zero-coded outcomes and shared-account-or-date CR0 covariance
remain in effect. No game downloads, API calls, engine runs, rating replay or
profile queries occur in production. If new comparison games genuinely lack
cached metadata, the branch writes OFFLINE_HOLD and preserves all other work.

RETURN THESE
The same consolidated desktop outputs are updated after each stage:
  MATERIAL_IV_BATCH_12093d55b7ee9f73_RETURN.zip
  MATERIAL_IV_BATCH_12093d55b7ee9f73_RETURN.zip.sha256
Return the ZIP and checksum when the launcher finishes. Private Parquets stay
on XT_Pro. BATCH_COMPLETE covers the named batch only; COVERAGE.json lists the
additional paper analyses and manuscript reconciliation still outstanding.

Optional verification without launching the unfinished analyses:
  bash "$HOME/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop/Mating_Material_IV_Resume_v1_0_1/RUN_IV_RESUME.command" --preflight-only

The production-sized repair cannot be run here because its data are on the
Mac. VALIDATION.json records the tests actually executed; REVIEW_RESULTS.txt
summarizes the verified partial results.
